        <ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.nature.com/articles/s43017-026-00828-5">
            <ns1:title>Rethinking ocean alkalinity enhancement</ns1:title>
            <ns1:link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s43017-026-00828-5</ns1:link>
            <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature Reviews Earth &amp;amp; Environment, Published online: 06 October 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s43017-026-00828-5"&gt;doi:10.1038/s43017-026-00828-5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Ocean alkalinity enhancement (OAE) is often thought of as a global-scale geoengineering approach to mitigate climate change. This Perspective explores the environmental effects, geochemical constraints, verification and governance of OAE and argues for local-scale, context-led evaluation.</content:encoded>
            <dc:title>Rethinking ocean alkalinity enhancement</dc:title>
            <dc:creator>Lennart T. Bach</dc:creator><dc:creator>Dariia Atamanchuk</dc:creator><dc:creator>Damon Britton</dc:creator><dc:creator>Michael Fuhr</dc:creator><dc:creator>Astrid Hylén</dc:creator><dc:creator>Sara Nawaz</dc:creator><dc:creator>Tyler Rohr</dc:creator>
            <dc:identifier>doi:10.1038/s43017-026-00828-5</dc:identifier>
